Incident: final Control-sync bundle creation rejected a raw positive commit ID
Date: 2026-08-29
Scope: local bundle preparation only; no server contact or mutation occurred

Observed error:

    fatal: Refusing to create empty bundle.

Cause:

`git bundle create` was given the target only as a raw positive commit ID and
the source as a negative prerequisite. Bundle creation requires the included
tip to be named by a ref; the equivalent raw revision expression produced no
advertised reference and Git rejected the bundle.

Safe correction:

Use the already fetched and verified `origin/control-main` ref as the positive
tip, retain the exact prior canonical server commit as the negative
prerequisite, then run `git bundle verify`, SHA-256 and byte-size checks before
any transfer. The target commit/tree must still be independently compared with
the canonical post-merge values.

Impact and rollback:

No bundle was created, transferred or imported. No server file, ref, worktree,
service or runtime state changed. There is therefore nothing to roll back.
